\par
Calendar TODO \u8212? third-party notices for the Windows distribution\par
================================================================\par
\par
This file accompanies the Calendar TODO Windows application and its installers. It lists the\par
third-party components that are contained in the distributed artifacts, with their licenses.\par
\par
Distribution scope\par
------------------\par
* 297 dependency entries cover the Windows normal-dependency closure and the\par
  packages emitted into the static frontend. Link-time elimination may omit some code; proc\par
  macros generate code rather than executing in the installed app. Their notices are retained.\par
* Components that are used only while building the project (Rust build scripts and the npm\par
  bundler toolchain, including Vite, Rolldown, SvelteKit build tooling, TypeScript and the\par
  Tauri CLI) are not contained in the distributed artifacts and are therefore not reproduced\par
  here. Their terms are recorded in the source repository notice file.\par
* The NSIS installer engine and its bundled plugins are contained in the NSIS installer.\par
* The WiX Toolset build tooling produces the MSI; its licensing notice is reproduced below.\par
* The Microsoft Edge WebView2 SDK loader is statically linked into calendar-todo.exe; its\par
  license text is reproduced below. The WebView2 Runtime itself is not bundled.\par
\par
Notes on specific components\par
----------------------------\par
* Mozilla Public License 2.0 components (cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext,\par
  selectors) are used unmodified as dependencies. Exact versioned source archives are available\par
  below at no additional charge under MPL 2.0; the license text is reproduced in this file.\par
  cssparser 0.36.0: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/cssparser/0.36.0/download\par
  cssparser-macros 0.6.1: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/cssparser-macros/0.6.1/download\par
  dtoa-short 0.3.5: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/dtoa-short/0.3.5/download\par
  option-ext 0.2.0: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/option-ext/0.2.0/download\par
  selectors 0.36.1: https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/selectors/0.36.1/download\par
* Unicode-3.0 licensed components (ICU4X crates, tinystr, writeable, yoke, zerovec, zerotrie,\par
  litemap, potential_utf, zerofrom, unicode-ident) retain their Unicode copyright and terms.\par
* AWS-LC/BoringSSL/OpenSSL-derived code inside aws-lc-sys retains its original notices; the\par
  complete combined notice file from that crate is reproduced below.\par
* SQLite is in the public domain; the bundled libsqlite3-sys crate notice is reproduced below.\par
* The NSIS plugins shipped inside the setup program (System.dll, nsDialogs.dll, StartMenu.dll,\par
  NSISdl.dll) come from the NSIS distribution and are covered by the NSIS notice below;\par
  nsis_tauri_utils.dll comes from github.com/tauri-apps/nsis-tauri-utils; its MIT text is\par
  retained separately below. The NSIS LZMA component retains CPL-1.0 with its linking\par
  exception; WiX components retain MS-RL. The application MIT license does not replace them.\par
  The accompanying CalendarTODO-installer-sources-0.1.0.zip contains the exact NSIS 3.11,\par
  WiX 3.14.1 and nsis-tauri-utils 0.5.3 source snapshots, their licenses, generated installer\par
  inputs with machine paths normalized, and a component correspondence record. Obtain it\par
  alongside the installer from the same distribution location, at no additional charge.\par
  Distribute that archive together with these installers. No differing terms for the covered\par
  components are offered by Calendar TODO. Any separate project provisions are offered by\par
  the project alone and not by upstream contributors.\par
  Upstream sources: https://sourceforge.net/projects/nsis/files/ and\par
  https://github.com/wixtoolset/wix3/tree/wix3141rtm\par
\par
Microsoft Edge WebView2\par
------------------------\par
The application displays its interface using the Microsoft Edge WebView2 Runtime, which is a\par
Microsoft component installed and serviced separately from this application. This distribution\par
does not bundle the WebView2 Runtime or its bootstrapper. The v0.1.0 NSIS and MSI installers\par
skip Runtime installation: they do not download or execute a Microsoft Runtime installer.\par
The Runtime must already be installed for the application interface to work. If it is missing,\par
use Microsoft's official page and follow Microsoft's Runtime installation instructions:\par
https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/webview2/\par
Review the terms presented by Microsoft. Calendar TODO neither supplies replacement Microsoft\par
license text nor asserts the user's acceptance. This notice does not grant rights to Microsoft software.\par
\par
The WebView2 SDK loader (WebView2LoaderStatic.lib from the Microsoft.Web.WebView2 NuGet\par
package, version 1.0.3650.58, as redistributed by the webview2-com-sys 0.38.2 crate and\par
confirmed byte-identical to that package) is statically linked into calendar-todo.exe; the\par
executable has no WebView2Loader.dll dependency. Its BSD-3-Clause license is reproduced below.\par
The exact SDK package NOTICE.txt is retained below. Its package-wide references to\par
Antlr3.Runtime and StringTemplate4 do not establish that those assemblies are shipped here;\par
they are retained as upstream notice context without asserting their presence in the loader.\par
\par
Microsoft Windows SDK and Visual C++ runtime\par
--------------------------------------------\par
The application is built with the Microsoft Windows SDK and MSVC toolchain. It links the Windows\par
API and the Universal C Runtime through operating-system components (api-ms-win-crt-* and the\par
Windows DLLs listed in its import table). No Microsoft redistributable runtime DLL is copied into\par
the installer. Microsoft Windows SDK redistributable file lists are published at\par
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/legal/windows-sdk/redist and apply only to files actually\par
redistributed. Absence of a separate runtime DLL does not exclude statically linked support\par
code or by itself establish compliance with Microsoft redistribution conditions.\par
\par
